From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Initialize the contact stream iterator without patches

PxContactStreamIterator leaves its patch, contact and face index pointers
uninitialized when constructed from a null patch stream, and its
hasNextPatch() only looks at the patch count, so a caller that trusts the
count can read them. GCC also sees this through the inlining and reports
it as a maybe-uninitialized use in code that includes the header with
warnings as errors.

This is the PhysX 4.1 patch "Workaround maybe-uninitialized error in GCC
12.2.1", forward ported to 5.9.0, where PxContact.h is unchanged in this
respect.

Task-number: QTBUG-108045
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/PxContact.h | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/PxContact.h b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/PxContact.h
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/PxContact.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/PxContact.h
@@ -325,7 +325,12 @@ struct PxContactStreamIterator
 
 			response = (patch->internalFlags & PxContactPatch::eFORCE_NO_RESPONSE) == 0;
 		}
-
+		else
+		{
+			patch = NULL;
+			contact = NULL;
+			faceIndice = NULL;
+		}
 
 		mStreamFormat = compressedModify ? eCOMPRESSED_MODIFIABLE_STREAM : modify ? eMODIFIABLE_STREAM : eSIMPLE_STREAM;
 		hasFaceIndices = PxU32(indices);
